  "answer": "Evidence: `prash/server.py:L704-L722`. - [implemented] `POST /api/chat/execute` (`execute_chat_action`) turns a JSON `command` list (or an action id) into CLI arguments, prefixing `run` when the first word is not a known subcommand, and re-enters `cli.build_parser()` in the same process. [1] Reversible: True. - Class: `TerraformInitAction` at `prash/actions/terraform_init.py:L16-L78`; spec at `prash/actions/terraform_init.py:L17-L23`. - Registered in the CLI dispatcher: yes. - Contract methods defined in the class: execute, plan, verify. - Summary (from the spec): Run terraform init to download modules and providers. - Capabilities: `('init',)`. [4]",
